1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,237
In the final lesson of
the Contacts module,

2
00:00:03,237 --> 00:00:05,847
you'll learn to keep your database clean.

3
00:00:05,847 --> 00:00:09,730
We'll group people under companies,
merge duplicate contacts,

4
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:12,850
and bring back anyone who
was deleted by mistake.

5
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:17,369
A clean database means accurate
reports, and automations you can trust.

6
00:00:18,225 --> 00:00:19,927
Let's start with Companies.

7
00:00:19,927 --> 00:00:24,845
If you work with businesses, a company
record groups everyone who works there.

8
00:00:24,845 --> 00:00:28,879
Bloom, for example, runs staff
dental plans for local employers.

9
00:00:29,729 --> 00:00:31,564
To add one, click Add Company.

10
00:00:31,564 --> 00:00:34,866
Fill in the name, phone
number and website, then save.

11
00:00:34,866 --> 00:00:38,290
You can add the address and
an owner from your team too.

12
00:00:39,523 --> 00:00:44,938
Open a company to see its details, the
people linked to it, and its opportunities,

13
00:00:44,938 --> 00:00:46,061
all in one place.

14
00:00:46,061 --> 00:00:50,750
Here's Marylebone Law, a local firm
whose staff get 10% off with Bloom.

15
00:00:51,599 --> 00:00:55,472
To link someone, click Add contact
and pick them from the list.

16
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:57,932
You can link as many people as you like.

17
00:00:57,932 --> 00:01:02,912
Now, when Noah calls, your team can see
straight away that he's on the Marylebone

18
00:01:02,912 --> 00:01:03,834
Law staff plan.

19
00:01:04,684 --> 00:01:05,736
Now, duplicates.

20
00:01:05,736 --> 00:01:07,315
They happen to everyone.

21
00:01:07,315 --> 00:01:12,250
Olivia filled in a Facebook form, then
later chatted on our website as Liv,

22
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:13,763
with a different email.

23
00:01:13,763 --> 00:01:16,986
Kyntlo had no way to know
it was the same person.

24
00:01:16,986 --> 00:01:20,671
Search by surname, and both
records appear side by side.

25
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,756
Tick both contacts.

26
00:01:22,756 --> 00:01:27,767
When exactly two are selected, a Merge
button appears in the bulk action bar.

27
00:01:27,767 --> 00:01:33,038
You can only merge two contacts at a time,
which keeps it safe and easy to check.

28
00:01:33,892 --> 00:01:34,657
Click Merge.

29
00:01:34,657 --> 00:01:37,911
First, choose which contact
to keep as the primary.

30
00:01:37,911 --> 00:01:40,781
Then, for each field,
pick the value to keep.

31
00:01:40,781 --> 00:01:45,694
We'll keep Olivia's full first name,
her original email and her phone number.

32
00:01:46,545 --> 00:01:49,737
Tags are combined, and
the conversations, notes,

33
00:01:49,737 --> 00:01:53,395
tasks and appointments from
both records come together.

34
00:01:53,395 --> 00:01:56,787
Merging can't be undone,
so take a moment to check.

35
00:01:56,787 --> 00:01:58,517
Then click Merge contacts.

36
00:01:59,366 --> 00:02:03,795
And now there's just one Olivia, with
her complete history in one place.

37
00:02:03,795 --> 00:02:08,348
Your reports count her once, and your
automations won't message her twice.

38
00:02:09,197 --> 00:02:10,313
Finally, Restore.

39
00:02:10,313 --> 00:02:15,568
If someone deletes a contact by mistake,
open the Restore tab, find the contact,

40
00:02:15,568 --> 00:02:16,750
and click Restore.

41
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:21,085
Charlotte is back on your
contact list, with her history.

42
00:02:21,085 --> 00:02:25,243
So before you re-create someone by
hand, always check Restore first.

43
00:02:25,243 --> 00:02:29,584
Restoring keeps their original history,
which a new record never could.

44
00:02:30,435 --> 00:02:31,462
Here's a pro tip.

45
00:02:31,462 --> 00:02:36,055
Once a month, search your list for
common surnames and check for duplicates.

46
00:02:36,055 --> 00:02:39,560
Merge them, and link business
contacts to their companies.

47
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:43,428
Ten minutes a month keeps your
reports and automations accurate.

48
00:02:44,277 --> 00:02:46,833
That's the end of the Contacts module.

49
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:47,505
Well done!

50
00:02:47,505 --> 00:02:50,667
Next, in module four,
we'll open Conversations,

51
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:55,106
the unified inbox where every
email, text and chat comes together.

52
00:02:55,106 --> 00:02:56,047
See you there.
